{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1352699-playing-out-the-awakening-crafting-covert-choices","id":1352699,"title":"Playing out the awakening - crafting covert choices","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-04T16:53:55-08:00","id":1352699,"title":"Playing out the awakening - crafting covert choices","content":"I have a team of 7 players who will each be awakening next session. Since it has been a thrill to do it in the first edition, I plan on running it classically: they each \u201ctravel\u201d to their path\u2019s realm, traverse to their respective towers, and forms a sympathetic connection to it. To that end though, I would like them to make choices and face challenges that manifest in mechanical consequences. Specifically, they\u2019ll exit with one dot in one ruling arcana and 2 dots in another*. <br /> <br /> One I already have in mind is this. <br /> Moros - \u201cYou continue down the path. As you do, the density of the pitch-black woods increases, and though they have no leaves, the enclosure is now so perfect that you can\u2019t walk off the forest path even if you tried; a matter that becomes an issue when you reach a dead end. Looking up, you still see the watchtower above the tree lines. You see it\u2019s ghostly white light and the gentle hum has grown stronger as you have approach. Something moves to your left out of the corner of your eye. Where you know there was once a tight knit wall of trees, you now see an opening covered with bramble and thorns. In front of it stands a frail old beggar extending his hand. \u201cWill you give your wealth to benefit the living?\u201d. Before you can act, you hear a voice behind you saying, \u201cOr will your efforts be to vouchsafe the dead?\u201d. As you turn, you see a hollow ferryman standing over a funeral boat. In the boat lies a corpse with one coin covering one eye. Behind them you also see an opening, this one leading to a river that passes through the forest. Your guide from earlier only gave you a single gold coin. What do you do?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mechanically, if he gives the coin to the beggar, he is \u201cchoosing\u201d to emphasis matter; his choice is to grant material wealth to the living. Alternatively, he can help the corpse pay the ferryman; his choice is to honor the dead. One will have him return with 2 dots in matter and the other will have him return with 2 dots of death, respectively.<br /> <br /> So I turn now to this forum for more inspiration. I need to pull a stunt like this 7 times in total. I already have a few handy, but I could use some more ideas and inspiration. Hell, for some paths, I gotta do this more than once. Any ideas of how I can make symbolic choices between the two arcana for the other paths?<br /> <br /> *I know this is less than CC RAW. But I am hoping to not overwhelm my players, as part of this game will be them learning everything in-game. In essence, they aren\u2019t reading the book because part of the fun will be them discovering its content through gameplay. Hence the \u201cdumb down\u201d amount of arcana dots. They will be granted all their owed dots for free in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:26:11-08:00","id":1352716,"title":"","content":"You should probably account for them taking a third option: &quot;This coin will help this person before me, but the dead must also be respected. I shall grant you this coin so you may survive. Use it wisely and your riches will multiply, when they do, I hope you will also extend a kind hand to pay for the burial of this person.&quot; In this case the player technically solved both problems by having faith in the beggar, by taking a chance, so that could grant him a point in Fate.<br /> <br /> <i>Acanthus</i><br /> <br /> At this point the thorns in your arms have become mirrors, each a lens revealing a new age, each age needing but a thought to let you cross into it (see the timepiece in Dishonored 2 for an idea of what this looks like). The path marches on through cambodian cities to victorian mansions, from phoenician ports to jungle caves, passing through tropical island nations and steppe tribes. Each jump changes your face, your voice, your memories, but only now do they all have one thing in common: they move with a stride that carries certain purpose, continuing down the path unrelentingly. Each a past life, some certain of their path, others bound by it, some lifetimes wasted, others glorious. But now your path threads further, away from normal time, you see visions and voices, they are faint, like murmurs in a theater, but you can almost understand a bit of it: (This is where you foreshadow a big Mystery/prophecy/event).<br /> <br /> You just arrived at a bountiful field, extending as far as the eye can see and you are lulled into a profound stillness. From you emerge a thousand clones, like echoes given shape, then substance. Each is a past, alternative or a possible life. You watch them build a civilization, give birth, die, see it flourish and fall to ruin, paying attention to every moment for what feels like thousands of years.<br /> <br /> You watch this cycle of rebirth a thousand times, each kingdom taking the knowledge of the previous one step further. Suddenly you notice a kindly old man in a robe is watching alongside you. He tells you &quot;I shall give you a gift to remember us by, but to pick the right one I must know, what defines our people to you ? How they live their lives or what they leave for future generations ?&quot; Choosing the first grants them Fate and the second one grants Time. The different gifts are a way of choosing their Dedicated Tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-05-2019, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:56:51-08:00","id":1352724,"title":"","content":"I would highly recommend <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, it covers Awakening in greater detail than the core book (incidentally, 2&amp;1 in ruling is what newly Awakened start with, the core character creation represents Mages that have been active for several months).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T00:24:10-08:00","id":1352767,"title":"","content":"And if you have access to Signs of sorcery i would suggest considering the option of one or more Entangled awakenings (essentialy two mages awakening in the same moment and in the same trial) because you have so many players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T06:27:05-08:00","id":1352799,"title":"","content":"<i>Obrimos</i><br /> <br /> Your path leads you through a dense mist, most of it sky blue, some of it aglow with dust particles. In the distance you see a drifting star, its light a golden glow, like a lighthouse in the darkness.<br /> <br /> As you draw close, you realize its an inverted island of impossible beauty. You feel a sense of nostalgia, like you are supposed to be there. An inner light begins to shine from within you. The mists part and you realize you were on the night sky. It and the glowing particles rearrange into a new path of stardust, leading you to the island, like a shooting star being drawn to the earth.<br /> <br /> The island is unlike anything you have ever seen. Life and matter form a continuous cycle, houses become birds, birds become trees, trees become waterfalls, flowers become flying whales. On it goes, every being reshaping this smelting aura that composes them into a myriad of wondrous forms. Above the weather changes in a symphony of nature, from auroras to thunderstorms of a thousand colors, from cyclones inhabited with flying fish to volcanoes that spew chilling lava. Life is not harmed by this, it only adapts. There is no death here, only reforged purpose, as if it was was a perfectly calibrated and free flowing mechanism.<br /> <br /> Suddenly you see a king beside you. He wears no regalia, yet he needs no crown, scepter or throne. His presence alone instills a sense of deep wisdom and kindness. All that stands out beside that is his cloak, weaved from stars. But you feel it was given by a grateful cosmos.<br /> <br /> He speaks to you, his voice certain and sure, yet powerful like thunder &quot;Welcome back home, this is the way things truly are. This is the true glory of creation, laid bare for you to see, free of their (points at the distance) cruelty&quot;<br /> <br /> You see something disturbing in the horizon. Living shadow and balefire, stepping across blood rivers with a thousand wailing faces, all bound with blazing hot chains. Looking upon them you feel like they wish to snuff out every light in the firmament, to bind the island in eternal torment.<br /> <br /> His eyes are fixed on them, showing unassailable courage. The Star Cloaked King of Thunder speaks once more: &quot;Stand tall, champion ! If we are to protect this land, then you must be my strength. If you are to be my strength, then you must wield the might of this kingdom. I can grant you the smelting aura of this land, to allow you to forge victory itself with you very hands. Alternatively, you can wield the storm at the core of heaven and earth, to burn away this corruption yourself. Mighty paragon, choose the armament you will bear.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first choice grants Prime, second grants Forces. Its also easy enough to expand into multiple Awakenings, as a company of heroes taking on the fight. The battle is where you determine their Dedicated Tools by how they wield their weapons. The actions of the Exarchs/Scelestus/Banisher army will act as a symbolic foreshadowing of their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-05-2019, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T08:21:06-08:00","id":1352816,"title":"","content":"I also recommend throwing the occasional &quot;coincidence&quot; during the campaign. If they see posters, tv shows, ephemeral incidents and alike that bear resemblance to their Awakenings, it reinforces the themes of the campaign. It is not as powerful or binding as a Destiny, but perhaps the Supernal or even the Oracles are trying to tell them something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}